            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32289",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-32289"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-32289?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.25.9",
              "help": {
                "text": "Context was not properly tracked across template branches for JS template literals, leading to possibly incorrect escaping of content when branches were used. Additionally template actions within JS template literals did not properly track the brace depth, leading to incorrect escaping being applied.\n\nThese issues could cause actions within JS template literals to be incorrectly or improperly escaped, leading to XSS vulnerabilities.\n",
                "markdown": "> Context was not properly tracked across template branches for JS template literals, leading to possibly incorrect escaping of content when branches were used. Additionally template actions within JS template literals did not properly track the brace depth, leading to incorrect escaping being applied.\n\nThese issues could cause actions within JS template literals to be incorrectly or improperly escaped, leading to XSS vulnerabilities.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.19.7  |\n|Affected range  <1.25.9                   |\n|Fixed version   1.25.9                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.25.9",
                "cvssV3_severity": "UNSPECIFIED",
                "fixed_version": "1.25.9",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.19.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "UNSPECIFIED"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-27139",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-27139"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-27139?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.25.8",
              "help": {
                "text": "On Unix platforms, when listing the contents of a directory using File.ReadDir or File.Readdir the returned FileInfo could reference a file outside of the Root in which the File was opened.\n\nThe impact of this escape is limited to reading metadata provided by lstat from arbitrary locations on the filesystem without permitting reading or writing files outside the root.\n",
                "markdown": "> On Unix platforms, when listing the contents of a directory using File.ReadDir or File.Readdir the returned FileInfo could reference a file outside of the Root in which the File was opened.\n\nThe impact of this escape is limited to reading metadata provided by lstat from arbitrary locations on the filesystem without permitting reading or writing files outside the root.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.19.7  |\n|Affected range  <1.25.8                   |\n|Fixed version   1.25.8                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.25.8",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "1.25.8",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.19.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "2.5",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22873",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-22873"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-22873?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.23.9",
              "help": {
                "text": "It was possible to improperly access the parent directory of an os.Root by opening a filename ending in \"../\". For example, Root.Open(\"../\") would open the parent directory of the Root. This escape only permits opening the parent directory itself, not ancestors of the parent or files contained within the parent.\n",
                "markdown": "> It was possible to improperly access the parent directory of an os.Root by opening a filename ending in \"../\". For example, Root.Open(\"../\") would open the parent directory of the Root. This escape only permits opening the parent directory itself, not ancestors of the parent or files contained within the parent.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.19.7  |\n|Affected range  <1.23.9                   |\n|Fixed version   1.23.9                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.23.9",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "1.23.9",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.19.7"
