            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-58183",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-58183"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-58183?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.24.8",
              "help": {
                "text": "tar.Reader does not set a maximum size on the number of sparse region data blocks in GNU tar pax 1.0 sparse files. A maliciously-crafted archive containing a large number of sparse regions can cause a Reader to read an unbounded amount of data from the archive into memory. When reading from a compressed source, a small compressed input can result in large allocations.\n",
                "markdown": "> tar.Reader does not set a maximum size on the number of sparse region data blocks in GNU tar pax 1.0 sparse files. A maliciously-crafted archive containing a large number of sparse regions can cause a Reader to read an unbounded amount of data from the archive into memory. When reading from a compressed source, a small compressed input can result in large allocations.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.19.7  |\n|Affected range  <1.24.8                   |\n|Fixed version   1.24.8                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.24.8",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "1.24.8",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.19.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.3",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22870",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-22870: Misinterpretation of Input"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-22870?s=github&n=net&ns=golang.org%2Fx&t=golang&vr=%3C0.36.0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Matching of hosts against proxy patterns can improperly treat an IPv6 zone ID as a hostname component. For example, when the NO_PROXY environment variable is set to \"*.example.com\", a request to \"[::1%25.example.com]:80` will incorrectly match and not be proxied.\n",
                "markdown": "> Matching of hosts against proxy patterns can improperly treat an IPv6 zone ID as a hostname component. For example, when the NO_PROXY environment variable is set to \"*.example.com\", a request to \"[::1%25.example.com]:80` will incorrectly match and not be proxied.\n\n|                                                                                                                  |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:golang/golang.org/x/net@0.2.0  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <0.36.0                            |\n|Fixed version                                                                  0.36.0                             |\n|[[CVSS Score 4.4] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:L]]                                     |\n"
